	void coreStripsToTenDigits() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
		o.put("telephone", "(04) 1234-5678");
		int id = createOwnerOk(o);
		getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("0412345678"));
	}

	@Test
	void errorRejectsTooFewDigits() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
		o.put("telephone", "12345");
		createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
	}
}
```
Test 1 sends `"(04) 1234-5678"` (12 digits after stripping non-digits: `0412345678` — actually that strips to `0412345678`, 10 digits) and expects the stored/returned value `"0412345678"`. Test 2 sends `"12345"` and expects **400**.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the harness. Key helpers:
- `ownerNode()` builds a valid owner using `uniqueTelephone()` → `String.format("04%08d", seq())` (a 10-digit AU mobile).
- `createOwner(body)` → `POST /api/owners`; `createOwnerOk(body)` asserts 2xx and extracts `id`; `getOwner(id)` → `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

Note: `getOwner` reads back through `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` (`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`), so the normalized value must be persisted, not just returned on create. `AuditLogCapture.java` also exists in that package but is unrelated.

---

## 6. Build file & OfficeFloor starter

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`**. The OfficeFloor Spring Boot starter **is present**:
```xml
<officefloor.version>4.0.2</officefloor.version>
...
<dependency>
    <groupId>net.officefloor.springboot</groupId>
    <artifactId>officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter</artifactId>
    <version>${officefloor.version}</version>
</dependency>
```
Also `net.officefloor.web` (v4.0.2) and the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (v7.23.0) which generates the DTOs/APIs from `openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` (apiPackage `...rest.api`, modelPackage `...rest.dto`). A build-helper adds that generated folder as a source root.

---

## 7. Validation / 400 escalation handlers

Registered escalations under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`:

- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.RequiredFieldsException.yml` → handler `RequiredFieldsExceptionHandler`
- `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` → handler `ValidationExceptionHandler`
- `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` → `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler`
- `java.lang.Exception.yml` → `GeneralExceptionHandler`
- plus `NotFoundException.yml` and `AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`

### The two relevant to a telephone 400:

**`RequiredFieldsException.java`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/RequiredFieldsException.java`) — a checked `Exception` carrying a `List<String> errors` (offending field names). This is what `RequireOwnerFields` throws.

**`RequiredFieldsExceptionHandler.java`** — maps it to HTTP 400:
```java
public class RequiredFieldsExceptionHandler {
    public void handle(@Parameter RequiredFieldsException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ValidationErrorsResponse>> response) {
        response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
                .body(new ValidationErrorsResponse(ex.getErrors())));
    }
}
```
Response body shape: `{"errors": ["telephone", ...]}` via `ValidationErrorsResponse` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/ValidationErrorsResponse.java`).

**`ValidationExceptionHandler.java`** — handles bean/schema validation failures (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`) into an RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` with a `schemaValidationErrors` list, also HTTP 400. This is what fires if the generated-DTO `@Pattern`/`@Size` (from the OpenAPI schema) rejects the body.

### Implementation guidance implied by the code

To satisfy the two tests: the cleanest fit is to strip non-digits and enforce exactly 10 digits inside the create-validation stage (`RequireOwnerFields`, or a dedicated new step before `BuildOwner`) and set the normalized value back onto the DTO so `BuildOwner`/the mapper persists and returns it. You must ensure the OpenAPI `telephone` schema pattern (`^[0-9]*$`, currently rejecting `(`, spaces, `-`) does not 400 the raw input via `MethodArgumentNotValidException` **before** your normalization runs — either relax that pattern in `openapi.yml` or perform normalization ahead of schema validation. Throwing `RequiredFieldsException` (or a similar escalation) yields the 400 for the "not exactly 10 digits" case (test `errorRejectsTooFewDigits`).

